# Corruption detection floors for ./corruption-coverage --floors.
# See docs/corruption_coverage.md for what the numbers mean.
#
# The campaign is deterministic: the same master seed, trial count,
# corruption-reader version and tiffz build give the same detections.
# A floor is the detection count measured when it was last set, so any
# lost detection fails ./test. Raise a floor when detection improves.
# Lower one only on purpose, saying in the commit why tiffz now accepts
# those cases (for example, a deviation reclassified as tolerated).
#
# Classes by integrity protection, weakest first: uncompressed (worst
# case: every value is a legal sample), unchecked (compressed without an
# integrity check) and checksummed (best case: Deflate or LERC).
# Set 2026-10-28 with corruption-reader 0.8.0 (a7ea995), 385 decisive
# trials per profile. Raised 2026-11-03 for findings 17 and 18 (IFD-entry
# rules): sniper +6/+1/+1, bolter +3/+0/+1.

